  "rawText": "She married Vernal Davis and continued to make her home in\nWashington, D.C.. In 1950, when her sister, Eula Mae, became\n111 and could not care for her infant son, Exrtie Lee took over\nhis care. Eula Mae passed away in October of that same year\nand the baby (Woody) was left with Extie Lee and Vernal\npermanently.\n\nIn the mid sixties, when Woody was old enough to be left\nalone aftex school, Extie Lee accepted a position with The\nDepartment of The United States Treasury.\n\nEven though, she retained her membership in Daniel Chapel\n\nBabtist Church, she was very active in several churches in the\nWashington area. |\n\nShe and Vernal moved to their new home in Enfield,\nNorth Carolina, in 1980. He passed away in 1987, and she\nfollowed him in 1991.\n\nHer goal in life was to be a good Christian.\n\nFront Row: Robert Calvin, Extie Lee, Maurice\nBack Row: Mattie, Pearl C. Eula Mae and Lillie Bell (Sweet)",
  "cleanedText": "She married Vernal Davis and continued to make her home in\nWashington, D.C.. In 1950, when her sister, Eula Mae, became\n111 and could not care for her infant son, Exrtie Lee took over\nhis care. Eula Mae passed away in October of that same year\nand the baby (Woody) was left with Extie Lee and Vernal\npermanently.\n\nIn the mid sixties, when Woody was old enough to be left\nalone aftex school, Extie Lee accepted a position with The\nDepartment of The United States Treasury.\n\nEven though, she retained her membership in Daniel Chapel\n\nBabtist Church, she was very active in several churches in the\nWashington area. I\n\nShe and Vernal moved to their new home in Enfield,\nNorth Carolina, in 1980. He passed away in 1987, and she\nfollowed him in 1991.\n\nHer goal in life was to be a good Christian.\n\nFront Row: Robert Calvin, Extie Lee, Maurice\nBack Row: Mattie, Pearl C. Eula Mae and Lillie Bell (Sweet)",
